  "term": "Dementia Rating Scale",
  "definition": "The Dementia Rating Scale, also called the Mattis Dementia Rating Scale, is a cognitive assessment used to measure overall cognitive functioning. In the supplied source, it is used as an outcome measure in studies of neuropsychological effects in Parkinson’s disease.",
